Corrected message:

Fix tautological key-binding tests and a weak transform guard test

- The three KeyDispatchTest default-gesture tests compared a binding
  with its own default and could not fail. They are replaced with
  override round trips: set a different key, expect it back, reset,
  expect the default.
- TransformToolZeroDivideGuardTest checked only that the transformed
  point was finite; it now checks the exact point, so a fallback to a
  wrong scale (0 or 0.5 instead of 1) fails.
